{"name":"Moon Shadow","hex":"#96a5b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Moon (“the Earth's only permanent natural satellite”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any natural satellite of a planet.","The light received from the Moon; moonlight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonshadow (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Moonshadow\" is a song written and performed by English musician Cat Stevens, first released as a single in the UK in 1970 on the Island label and in the US in June 1971 on the A&M label. It also appears on Stevens' 1971 album Teaser and the Firecat."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Moonshadow45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonshadow_(song)"},{"title":"Palisades Fire","blocks":[{"text":"The Palisades Fire was a highly destructive wildfire that began in the Santa Monica Mountains of Los Angeles County on January 7, 2025, and grew to destroy large areas of Pacific Palisades, Topanga, and Malibu before it was fully contained on January 31. One of a series of wildfires in Southern California driven by extremely powerful Santa Ana winds, it spread to 37 sq mi (95 km2), killed 12 people, and destroyed 6,837 structures, making it the tenth-deadliest and third-most destructive California wildfire on record and the second most destructive to occur in the history of the city of Los Angeles. The fire burned simultaneously with the similarly destructive Eaton Fire at the foothills of the nearby San Gabriel Mountains."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Homes_destroyed_in_the_Palisades_fire_%2854272193113%29.jpg/330px-Homes_destroyed_in_the_Palisades_fire_%2854272193113%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palisades_Fire"},{"title":"Moon Shadow (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Moon Shadow is the second album by American singing trio Labelle. This release was their second and last album for Warner Bros. Records. The album is notable for their soulful rendition of The Who's \"Won't Get Fooled Again\", the socially conscious \"I Believe That I've Finally Made It Home\" and the nine-minute title track in which Patti introduces all the musicians as they do their live solos. This is the first album where member Nona Hendryx begins taking over most of the songwriting."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/LabelleMoonShadow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_Shadow_(album)"},{"title":"Moon","blocks":[{"text":"The Moon is the only natural satellite of Earth. It orbits Earth in an elliptical path, at a distance that varies over the year, averaging around 378,000 kilometers (235,000 mi). It completes an orbit in relation to Earth and the Sun (synodically) every 29.5 days. The Moon and Earth are bound by gravitational attraction, which is stronger on the sides facing each other. The resulting tidal forces are the main driver of Earth's tides, and have pulled the Moon to always face Earth with the same near side. This tidal locking effectively synchronizes the Moon's rotation period to its orbital period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/330px-FullMoon2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg/500px-Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg/1280px-Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg/500px-Palisades_Fire_%2854257375328%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Chase Bank branch on Sunset Boulevard burning on January 8","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APalisades_Fire_(54257375328).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png/500px-20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png/1280px-20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png/500px-20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The fire on January 7, seen approximately three minutes after it was first reported","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20250107-palisades-fire-start-t-plus-three-min-ballona.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/